From 3e875d1a365f11e5470263506339410386ae7ae1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:19:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(ui): give the viewport bar buttons names no other
 control uses

The bar's accessible names "Display mode" and "Show all toolpaths"
were also the names of the Display menu group and the View menu
check box, so a query by name found two nodes. The Wire, Paths and
Projection buttons are now "Switch wireframe", "Show or hide
toolpaths" and "Switch projection"; the state text stays in the
tooltip. The label test checks that no name repeats.

Refs #2914

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
